  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: b9300cdd1a21ad44ba3fb44ddb8e9e37, type: 3}
  m_Name: TreeObstacleIntro
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  dialogue:
  - Transpiration is the process of water movement through a plant. About 97-99%
    of the water that plants absorb is lost through transpiration.
  - 'Water is absorbed at the roots, and then travels up through the plant. It reaches
    the leaves and exits as vapor through small pores, called stomata. '
  - That tree sapling ahead looks promising!
  - If the tree grows, you will be able to jump on top of it to reach higher places!
